          "id": "rate-calculation",
          "question": "Illustrative calculation: population 1,000; labour force 600; employed 540. Find LFPR and unemployment rate.",
          "answer": "LFPR = 600/1,000 = 60%. Unemployed = 600 - 540 = 60; unemployment rate = 60/600 = 10%. The numbers are invented for practice, not observed labour statistics.",
